Heeler: let the embedding host serve a config server's reverse RPC.

`easytier-core --config-server` registers EasyTier's whole process-management
RPC with the server: it can run any number of instances with any
configuration and hot-patch a running one (port forwards, subnet proxies, exit
nodes, mapped listeners, relay flags). Heeler's node only dials out, so it
serves its own, narrower surface instead, and checks every configuration a
server sends against the same outbound-only policy as a local one.

This patch only widens visibility and adds one constructor; no upstream
behaviour changes:
- `WebClientBackend` and `WebClient::with_backend`, already used by the WASI
  host, are public on every target;
- `easytier::web_client::run_web_client_with_backend` builds the
  config-server connector (udp, tcp, ws, wss) as `run_web_client` does and
  hands it to `with_backend` with an explicit machine ID.

Applies to EasyTier commit 728ba94b5029240add6204eed591f22e4e039e6b, after
0001, with `patch -p1 --fuzz=0`.

